[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:19. Sold Out]
[00:00.860]Passage 19 | 文章十九
[00:02.965]Sold out. | 票已售罄。
[00:06.200]The play may begin at any moment, I said. | 演出可能随时开始，我说。
[00:11.590]It may have begun already, Susan answered. | 可能已经开始了，苏珊回答。
[00:16.165]I hurried to the ticket office. | 我急忙赶到售票处。
[00:18.925]May I have two tickets, please? I asked. | 请给我两张票好吗？我问道。
[00:22.435]I'm sorry, we've sold out, the girl said. | 对不起，票已售罄，女孩说。
[00:26.990]What a pity, Susan exclaimed. | 多可惜啊！苏珊惊呼道。
[00:30.815]Just then, a man hurried to the ticket office. | 就在那时，一个男人急匆匆地赶到售票处。
[00:34.820]Can I return these two tickets? he asked. | 我能退这两张票吗？他问道。
[00:38.200]Certainly, the girl said. | 当然可以，女孩说。
[00:40.575]I went back to the ticket office at once. | 我立刻回到售票处。
[00:43.895]Could I have those two tickets, please? I asked. | 我能买那两张票吗？我问道。
[00:47.975]Certainly, the girl said. | 当然可以，女孩说。
[00:50.615]But they are for next Wednesday's performance. | 但那是下周三的演出。
[00:54.065]Do you still want them? | 你还要吗？
[00:56.590]I might as well have them, I said sadly. | 我还是买下它们吧，我悲伤地说。